    "### A4 · Python primer #2 — numbers, strings, f-strings (20–25 min)\n",
    "\n",
    "Two new ideas:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Arithmetic and types**: `+ - * / //  %  **`. `int(\"3\")` converts a string to a number.\n",
    "2. **f-strings**: a clean way to plug variables into text.\n",
    "\n",
    "Mini exercise at the end: a tip calculator."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Bill: RM 42.50\n",
      "Tip (10%): RM 4.25\n",
      "Total: RM 46.75\n",
      "<class 'float'> <class 'float'>\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Arithmetic and type conversion.\n",
    "bill = 42.50\n",
    "tip_pct = 10\n",
    "\n",
    "tip = bill * tip_pct / 100\n",
    "total = bill + tip\n",
    "\n",
    "# f-strings: prefix the string with f, put expressions in {}.\n",
    "print(f\"Bill: RM {bill:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Tip ({tip_pct}%): RM {tip:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total: RM {total:.2f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# What is the type of bill / tip?\n",
    "print(type(bill), type(tip))"
   ]
