    "## Part B · Guided exploration (60 min)\n",
    "\n",
    "### B1 · Code scenarios — combining Week 1 + Week 2 (20 min)\n",
    "Before the SDLC paper activities, two short coding scenarios that combine **everything you have met so far**: variables, `input()`, `print()`, ints/floats/strings, type conversion, arithmetic operators, and f-strings.\n",
    "\n",
    "Code each one **from scratch** in the cell beneath the description. You may use AI as a tutor (quiz you, explain a confusing line, suggest an idiom) but **not as a ghost-writer**. Every meaningful AI interaction goes into your AI Learning Log in Part C.\n",
    "\n",
    "Pseudocode it on paper first if it helps — three lines of plain English before you open the cell."
   ]
