  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### Scenario 1 — TnG eWallet receipt\n",
    "\n",
    "You just topped up your Touch 'n Go eWallet. After driving through one toll, the system deducts the toll and shows you a receipt.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Write a program that:**\n",
    "1. Asks the user for the **starting balance** in RM.\n",
    "2. Asks the user for the **toll amount** in RM.\n",
    "3. Computes the **remaining balance**.\n",
    "4. Prints a clean receipt using f-strings, with two decimal places everywhere.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected sample run** (`>` is your input):\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Starting balance (RM): > 50\n",
    "Toll amount (RM):      > 4.25\n",
    "\n",
    "--- TnG eWallet receipt ---\n",
    "Starting:   RM 50.00\n",
    "Toll:       RM  4.25\n",
    "Remaining:  RM 45.75\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hints you should already know:**\n",
    "- `input()` always returns a *string*. Convert with `float()` *before* doing arithmetic.\n",
    "- Format currency with `f\"RM {amount:.2f}\"`.\n",
    "- Right-align numbers inside a fixed width so the column lines up: `f\"{amount:>6.2f}\"`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stretch ideas (optional):**\n",
    "- If the toll is larger than the balance, print `INSUFFICIENT FUNDS — top up before the toll` instead of the receipt.\n",
    "- Add a top-up step that asks how much to add *before* the toll, then continues normally.\n",
    "- Save the program as `tng_receipt.py`."
   ]
  },
