    "#### Scenario 2 — Mamak bill splitter\n",
    "\n",
    "After a mamak session, you and your friends agreed to add a tip and split the bill evenly.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Write a program that:**\n",
    "1. Asks for the **bill amount** in RM.\n",
    "2. Asks for the **tip percentage** (e.g. `10` for 10%).\n",
    "3. Asks for the **number of people** splitting the bill.\n",
    "4. Computes the tip amount, grand total, and per-person share.\n",
    "5. Prints a clean itemised split using f-strings.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected sample run:**\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Bill amount (RM): > 48\n",
    "Tip percent (%):  > 10\n",
    "Number of people: > 4\n",
    "\n",
    "--- Mamak split ---\n",
    "Bill:            RM 48.00\n",
    "Tip (10%):       RM  4.80\n",
    "Grand total:     RM 52.80\n",
    "Per person (4):  RM 13.20\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hints you should already know:**\n",
    "- Tip percent is naturally a float (`10`, `7.5`); convert with `float()`.\n",
    "- Number of people is a *whole number*; convert with `int()`.\n",
    "- You can put arithmetic *inside* an f-string: `f\"{bill * tip_pct / 100:.2f}\"`.\n",
    "- The tip-percent label in the output uses the same variable: `f\"Tip ({tip_pct:g}%)\"` (the `:g` trick drops trailing zeros).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Stretch ideas (optional):**\n",
    "- Round the per-person amount **up** to the nearest sen so nobody underpays. Hint:\n",
    "  ```python\n",
    "  import math\n",
    "  per_person = math.ceil(per_person * 100) / 100\n",
    "  ```\n",
    "- If someone enters `0` for the number of people, print `Cannot split between 0 people — try again.` instead of crashing with `ZeroDivisionError`.\n",
    "- Save the program as `mamak_split.py`."
   ]
  },
