    "======### B3 · Twin-mode timed exercise (20 min)\n",
    "Same problem in two SDLC modes. The micro-problem: **a parking-permit request flow**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Mode A — Waterfall (10 min):** write the spec first, then a paper sketch.\n",
    "- Spec: \n",
    "Purpose: Let a resident request a parking permit online instead of offline. \n",
    "Actors: Applicant, staff.\n",
    "Functional requirements:\n",
    "1. Applicants enters name, email, vehicle plate number, address and permit type (resident or visitor).\n",
    "2. Applicant uploads proof of residence\n",
    "3. System validates required fields and plate format before submission.\n",
    "4. System shows a confirmation with a request ID.\n",
    "5. Reviewer approves or rejects with a reason.\n",
    "6. Applicant gets an confirmation email with the result.\n",
    "Rule: One active permit per plate, visitor permits last at most 7 days.\n",
    "Edge cases: Duplicate plate, wrong file type, rejection by reviewer, applicant edits after submission\n",
    "\n",
    "- Sketch (photo link): ![image.png](attachment:image.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Mode B — Iterative (10 min):** sketch first, get one round of feedback, revise.\n",
    "- Sketch v1 (photo link): ![image.png](attachment:image.png)_\n",
    "- One change after feedback: ___After the submission, how do I know it worked properly, description about a fee, Change: added a confirmation screen with request ID, Status, pending, email sent__\n",
    "- Sketch v2 (photo link): ![image-2.png](attachment:image-2.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reflection:** which felt better, for which kind of work? V2-more with information with working or not, description about a fee. "
   ]
